! Rising bubble of Fakhari, Geier & Lee, J. Comput. Phys. 315 (2016), Sec. 5.1,
! Figs. 3-5: rho_h/rho_l = 1000, mu_h/mu_l = 100, Re_h = 100, Pe = 1.1,
! Cn = 0.010, t* = 12, Eo = 20. Needs L0 = 512 (l_max = 6):
!   cmake -B build-paper -DAMR_L0=512 && cmake --build build-paper -j
!   AMR_CASE=cases/paper2016_Eo20.nml ./build-paper/amr_lbm
! (AMR_MODEL=pre2017 runs the same case with the PRE 2017 model)
! The gravity in lattice units is not given in the paper. It matters: the model is
! weakly compressible, so the bubble swells as it rises in the closed box (by ~25%
! at 2.5e-6, ~50% at 5e-6, proportional to Gy_lu). 2.5e-6 reproduces Fig. 4 best.
&run
  case  = 'rising_bubble'
  model = 'jcp2016'
/
&rising_bubble
  Eo        = 20
  Re        = 100
  rho_ratio = 1000
  mu_ratio  = 100
  Gy_lu     = 2.5e-6
  Pe        = 1.1
  Cn        = 0.010
  t_end     = 12
/
